============================================================
CODING AGENT EXECUTION RULES
============================================================

RULE 01:
Read the relevant locked documentation BEFORE implementing a phase.

RULE 02:
Inspect the actual repository BEFORE inventing files or code.

RULE 03:
Never assume a missing implementation means a new module is required.

RULE 04:
Use existing module ownership.

RULE 05:
Do not create duplicate responsibilities.

RULE 06:
Do not expand the module architecture.

RULE 07:
Do not modify locked documentation unless explicitly authorized.

RULE 08:
Do not introduce OpenCode into ATLAS runtime.

RULE 09:
Do not introduce MCP into ATLAS runtime.

RULE 10:
Treat model output as untrusted.

RULE 11:
Validate tool requests.

RULE 12:
Respect AT-16 permissions.

RULE 13:
Keep AI-08 verification separate from tool execution.

RULE 14:
Keep AI-07 task ownership.

RULE 15:
Keep AI-06 tool orchestration ownership.

RULE 16:
Keep AT modules responsible for capabilities.

RULE 17:
Keep UX modules responsible for UI/interaction.

RULE 18:
Keep REL-01 responsible for packaging/release.

RULE 19:
Do not claim something works without testing it.

RULE 20:
Do not claim a migration is complete without evidence.

RULE 21:
Do not invent APIs, schemas, IPC channels, commands, versions, or paths.

RULE 22:
Prefer inspecting existing code over guessing.

RULE 23:
After each meaningful implementation unit:

IMPLEMENT
→ TEST
→ VERIFY
→ COMMIT

RULE 24:
If a genuine architectural contradiction appears:

STOP
→ DOCUMENT THE CONFLICT
→ RESOLVE IT
→ CONTINUE

Do not silently change the architecture.

RULE 25:
Keep the repository recoverable through Git at all times.


============================================================
FINAL SUCCESS CONDITION
============================================================

ATLAS implementation is considered complete only when:

[ ] All locked modules are implemented to their defined responsibilities
[ ] UI is integrated
[ ] Runtime is integrated
[ ] AI is integrated
[ ] Data persistence works
[ ] IPC works
[ ] Security boundaries work
[ ] Integration tests pass
[ ] Production build passes
[ ] EXE works
[ ] MSI works
[ ] Windows installation works
[ ] Upgrade works
[ ] Uninstallation works
[ ] User data is preserved according to policy
[ ] Release checklist passes
[ ] Final Git state is recorded

FINAL RULE:

DO NOT EXPAND THE PLAN.

BUILD WHAT IS LOCKED.

IMPLEMENT → TEST → VERIFY → COMMIT.